/**

@page tutorials_exahype2_applications_exagrype_configure Configure ExaGRyPE

ExaGRyPE needs to be installed as an application of the Peano framework. For general remarks on
how to install Peano, please see \ref page_installation_home. This tutorial is also designed to be
self-contained, and thus should include all the steps you need to run the example code.

The code is still under active development in the repository at branch application-ccz4
(the name, which is not a good one, is subject to future change). To start, please clone
Peano and switch to the branch

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
git clone https://gitlab.lrz.de/hpcsoftware/Peano.git
git checkout applications-ccz4
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

then configure and compile Peano under the main directory as follows (please make sure that you load
the proper modules if you are working on a cluster such as COSMA, see \ref tutorials_exahype2_applications_exagrype_clusters)

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
libtoolize; aclocal; autoconf; autoheader; cp src/config.h.in .; automake --add-missing
./configure CC=icx CXX=icpx --with-mpi=mpiicpx --with-multithreading=omp CXXFLAGS="-Ofast -std=c++20 -qopenmp -march=native -mtune=native -fma -fomit-frame-pointer -Wno-attributes=clang:: -w" LDFLAGS="-qopenmp" --enable-loadbalancing --enable-exahype --enable-particles --enable-blockstructured --enable-finiteelements
make -j
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Missing certain installed libraries may lead to configuration/compilation errors; please check
\ref tutorials_exahype2_applications_exagrype_faq if necessary. Note you only need to compile Peano
once as long as your working environments and Peano kernel code are unchanged. And we recommend 
re-compiling it after you pull a new code version or change working environments (e.g., changing 
between different login nodes of a cluster)

The next step is to enter the ExaGRyPE subdirectory and add the Python path as

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
cd ./applications/exahype2/ccz4/
export PYTHONPATH=../../../python
export PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:../../../applications/exahype2/ccz4
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

ExaGRyPE requires three Python libraries that are usually not included in a standard
Python installation. You may install them separately using the Python pipeline.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
pip3 install jinja2 --user
pip3 install ast_comments --user
pip3 install vtk --user
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

also try

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
python3 -m pip install --user vtk --no-cache-dir
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

if \c pip3 does not work properly.

To clean the repository completely, use the following lines

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
rm -rf aclocal.m4 compile src/config.* configure *sh Makefile Makefile.in missing stamp* ar-lib autom4te.cache *.log libtool depcomp *.scan
find . -name Makefile -delete
find . -name Makefile.in -delete
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

*/

